{"step_index":890,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T18:13:38Z","input_tokens":2083,"cache_read_tokens":70154,"output_tokens":2437,"thinking":"The provided code attempts to sanitize a vendor name by removing trailing special characters and whitespace. It also suggests filtering \"garbage\" line items, though the implementation details of the filtering are not provided. The function aims to clean invoice data by removing noise from vendor names using a regular expression and implicitly suggests a method for filtering out unwanted line items.\n\n\nIterating through the items, the descriptions undergo cleaning: leading/trailing brackets and pipes are removed, and the description is stripped. Items are skipped if the description has too few letters, excessive symbols, or contains common footer terms. Quantity, rate, and total amount fields are also sanitized, converting commas and defaults to numeric values. Finally, the code ensures that numeric fields, such as \"subtotal\", \"cgst\", etc., correctly handle and remove commas from the vendor name as well.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"edit_file","args":{"Path":"/Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/clean_items.py","Replacement":"def sanitize_and_clean_invoice(data: dict) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sanitize and clean invoice data:\n    1. Clean supplier name of trailing symbols\n    2. Filter garbage line items (stamps, signatures, low letter count, excessive symbols)\n    3. Ensure numeric fields strip commas cleanly (e.g., '2,535.00' -> 2535.0)\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(data, dict):\n        return data\n\n    # 1. Clean supplier name of trailing symbols\n    supplier = data.get(\"vendor_name\") or data.get(\"supplier_name\") or \"\"\n    if supplier:\n        supplier_cleaned = re.sub(r'[\\s&0\\|\\[\\]\\(\\)]+$', '', str(supplier)).strip()\n        # Also clean phone/email prefixes if any\n        supplier_cleaned = re.sub(r'(Phone|Mobile|Tel|Email|Mob)[\\s:]*[\\+\\d\\s\\w@\\.\\-]+', '', supplier_cleaned, flags=re.IGNORECASE).strip()\n        supplier_cleaned = re.sub(r'[\\s,\\-–—:|]+$', '', supplier_cleaned).strip()\n        data[\"vendor_name\"] = supplier_cleaned if supplier_cleaned else \"Supplier Name Unclear\"\n        data[\"supplier_name\"] = data[\"vendor_name\"]\n\n    # 2. Filter garbage line items\n    clean_items = []\n    for item in data.get(\"items\", []):\n        if not isinstance(item, dict):\n            continue\n\n        desc = (item.get(\"description\") or \"\").strip()\n        \n        # Remove stray leading/trailing brackets and vertical pipes from OCR\n        desc = re.sub(r'^[\\[\\|\\]\\(\\)\\s]+|[\\[\\|\\]\\(\\)\\s]+$', '', desc).strip()\n        item[\"description\"] = desc\n\n        # Skip if description lacks at least 4 letters\n        if len(re.findall(r'[a-zA-Z]', desc)) < 4:\n            continue\n\n        # Skip if more than 20% of description is weird symbols/punctuation\n        symbols = re.findall(r'[~|©\\[\\]=_{}@#$%^&*]', desc)\n        if len(desc) > 0 and (len(symbols) / len(desc)) > 0.20:\n            continue\n\n        # Skip common footer/stamp terms\n        if any(term in desc.lower() for term in [\"signature\", \"authorised\", \"terms\", \"condition\", \"bank details\", \"e-way bill\"]):\n            continue\n\n        # Clean description: Do not append units like 'NO', 'PCS', 'NOS', etc.\n        desc_clean = re.sub(r'[\\s\\-,]+(NO|NOS|PCS|PIECES|PKT|PACKET|KG|BOX|SET)\\.?$', '', desc, flags=re.IGNORECASE).strip()\n        if desc_clean and len(desc_clean) >= 3:\n            desc = desc_clean\n            item[\"description\"] = desc\n\n        # Quantity and Rate sanity\n        try:\n            raw_qty = item.get(\"quantity\") if item.get(\"quantity\") is not None else item.get(\"qty\")\n            qty = float(str(raw_qty or 1).replace(\",\", \"\").strip())\n        except (ValueError, TypeError):\n            qty = 1.0\n\n        try:\n            raw_rate = item.get(\"unit_rate\") if item.get(\"unit_rate\") is not None else item.get(\"rate\", 0)\n            rate = float(str(raw_rate or 0).replace(\",\", \"\").strip())\n        except (ValueError, TypeError):\n            rate = 0.0\n\n        try:\n            raw_billed = item.get(\"total_amount\") if item.get(\"total_amount\") is not None else item.get(\"amount\")\n            billed = float(str(raw_billed if raw_billed is not None else (qty * rate)).replace(\",\", \"\").strip())\n        except (ValueError, TypeError):\n            billed = round(qty * rate, 2)\n\n        # Post-Processing Column Swap Fallback:\n        # If total matches qty exactly and rate is small (e.g. qty=535, rate=2, total=535), \n        # it means qty and rate were misaligned. Swap them:\n        if billed > 0 and qty == billed and rate in [1.0, 2.0, 1, 2]:\n            qty = 1.0\n            rate = billed\n\n        item[\"quantity\"] = qty\n        item[\"qty\"] = qty\n        item[\"unit_rate\"] = rate\n        item[\"rate\"] = rate\n        item[\"total_amount\"] = billed\n        item[\"amount\"] = billed\n        clean_items.append(item)\n\n    data[\"items\"] = clean_items\n\n    # 3. Ensure numeric fields strip commas cleanly\n    for key in [\"subtotal\", \"cgst\", \"sgst\", \"igst\", \"declared_total\"]:\n        val = data.get(key)\n        if val is not None and str(val).strip() != \"\" and str(val).lower() != \"null\":\n            try:\n                data[key] = float(str(val).replace(\",\", \"\").strip())\n            except (ValueError, TypeError):\n                pass\n\n    # Ensure schema aliases for frontend compatibility\n    if data.get(\"declared_total\") is not None:\n        data[\"total_declared\"] = data[\"declared_total\"]\n    elif data.get(\"total_declared\") is not None:\n        data[\"declared_total\"] = data[\"total_declared\"]\n\n    if data.get(\"invoice_number\") and not data.get(\"invoice_no\"):\n        data[\"invoice_no\"] = data[\"invoice_number\"]\n\n    return data\n\ndef sanitize_invoice_data(data: dict) -> dict:","Target":"def sanitize_invoice_data(data: dict) -> dict:"}}]}
