against the printed 'Amount/Total in Words' (e.g., 'FOUR THOUSAND FOUR HUNDRED AND NINETY RUPEES ONLY' means the total is 4490, not 2173).\n\n2. ONLY REAL PRODUCTS/SERVICES IN LINE ITEMS:\n   - Extract ONLY genuine products or services from the central invoice table (e.g., 'Bosch All-in-One Metal Hand Tool Kit', 'Taparia Universal Tool Kit').\n   - Clean the product description: strip table borders, brackets, or leading/trailing symbols like '[', '|', ']', or unit words like 'NOS'/'PCS'.\n   - NEVER extract rubber stamps, signatures, authorization seals, or hand scribbles (e.g., symbols like '©', '~', '|', '[', ']').\n\n3. GRAND TOTAL EXTRACTION:\n   - Look strictly for the final 'Grand Total', 'Total Amount', 'Net Payable', or 'कुल योग' at the bottom of the invoice (e.g., 4,490.00).\n   - DO NOT hallucinate the grand total by summing OCR misreads. Extract the actual printed total on the invoice.\n\n4. COLUMN INTEGRITY:\n   - Quantity is typically an integer (e.g., 1, 2, 5).\n   - Rate is the unit price (e.g., 2535.00, 1270.00).\n   - Billed Amount must reflect (Quantity * Unit Rate).\n\nExtract the invoice details into JSON matching this schema:\n- vendor_name: (string)\n- gstin: (string or null)\n- invoice_number: (string or null)\n- date: (string or null)\n- items: list of {description, quantity, unit_rate, total_amount}\n- subtotal: (number or null)\n- cgst: (number or null)\n- sgst: (number or null)\n- igst: (number or null)\n- declared_total: (number or null)\n\"\"\"","Target":"    # Prompt with table column alignment instructions\n    prompt = \"\"\"Extract the invoice details from this image/document into JSON:\n - vendor_name: (string)\n - gstin: (string or null)\n - invoice_number: (string or null)\n - items: list of {description, quantity, unit_rate, total_amount}\n - subtotal: (number)\n - cgst: (number)\n - sgst: (number)\n - igst: (number)\n - declared_total: (number)\n If any field is missing or unclear, leave it null. Do not include addresses or phone numbers as line items.\n\nTABLE COLUMN ALIGNMENT INSTRUCTIONS:\n- Carefully identify the table header row to locate column boundaries (S.No, Description, HSN/SAC, Quantity, Unit, Rate/Price, Amount).\n- CROSS-CHECK MATH INTERNALLY: For each row, verify that (quantity * unit_rate) roughly equals the row total amount. \n  * If quantity * rate does not equal the row amount, you likely swapped the Quantity and Rate columns, or confused the Item Code/HSN/S.No with Quantity. \n  * Never set Rate to trivial numbers like 1 or 2 when the item is an expensive product like a 'Tool Kit', unless that is explicitly the printed unit rate.\n- Clean description: Do not append units like 'NO', 'PCS', 'NOS', or serial numbers into the product description.\"\"\""}}]}
