e grand total by summing OCR misreads. Extract the actual printed total on the invoice.\n\n4. COLUMN INTEGRITY:\n   - Quantity is typically an integer (e.g., 1, 2, 5).\n   - Rate is the unit price (e.g., 2535.00, 1270.00).\n   - Billed Amount must reflect (Quantity * Unit Rate).\n\nReturn ONLY a valid JSON object matching this schema:\n{\n  \"vendor_name\": string or null,\n  \"gstin\": string or null,\n  \"invoice_number\": string or null,\n  \"date\": string or null,\n  \"items\": [\n    {\n      \"description\": string,\n      \"quantity\": number,\n      \"unit_rate\": number,\n      \"total_amount\": number\n    }\n  ],\n  \"subtotal\": number or null,\n  \"cgst\": number or null,\n  \"sgst\": number or null,\n  \"igst\": number or null,\n  \"declared_total\": number or null\n}\n`;","Target":"import { sanitizeInvoiceData } from \"./privacyMasker.js\";\nimport { parseInvoiceText, isLikelyInvoice } from \"./invoiceTextParser.js\";\nimport { cleanExtractedItems } from \"./itemCleaner.js\";\n\nconst DEFAULT_API_KEY = \"AQ.Ab8RN6LhTNa6kIQRpd_OijgrXNfmwLOw7rcxiMN8aWW-_U7mPw\";\n\nconst GEMINI_SYSTEM_INSTRUCTION = `Extract the invoice details from this image/document into JSON:\n - vendor_name: (string)\n - gstin: (string or null)\n - invoice_number: (string or null)\n - items: list of {description, quantity, unit_rate, total_amount}\n - subtotal: (number)\n - cgst: (number)\n - sgst: (number)\n - igst: (number)\n - declared_total: (number)\n If any field is missing or unclear, leave it null. Do not include addresses or phone numbers as line items.\n\nTABLE COLUMN ALIGNMENT INSTRUCTIONS:\n- Carefully identify the table header row to locate column boundaries (S.No, Description, HSN/SAC, Quantity, Unit, Rate/Price, Amount).\n- CROSS-CHECK MATH INTERNALLY: For each row, verify that (quantity * unit_rate) roughly equals the row total amount. \n  * If quantity * rate does not equal the row amount, you likely swapped the Quantity and Rate columns, or confused the Item Code/HSN/S.No with Quantity. \n  * Never set Rate to trivial numbers like 1 or 2 when the item is an expensive product like a 'Tool Kit', unless that is explicitly the printed unit rate.\n- Clean description: Do not append units like 'NO', 'PCS', 'NOS', or serial numbers into the product description.\n\nReturn ONLY a valid JSON object matching this schema:\n{\n  \"vendor_name\": string or null,\n  \"gstin\": string or null,\n  \"invoice_number\": string or null,\n  \"date\": string or null,\n  \"items\": [\n    {\n      \"description\": string,\n      \"quantity\": number,\n      \"unit_rate\": number,\n      \"total_amount\": number\n    }\n  ],\n  \"subtotal\": number or null,\n  \"cgst\": number or null,\n  \"sgst\": number or null,\n  \"igst\": number or null,\n  \"declared_total\": number or null\n}\n`;"}}]}
